    "details": "<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Edge AI Challenge</strong> is a team-based technical competition focused on TinyML, Edge Computing and Embedded AI. Participants will receive a common Edge AI problem statement, dataset, target-platform specifications and submission requirements at the beginning of the competition.</p>\n<p>Teams of 2&ndash;3 members will have <strong>2 hours</strong> to develop, train, validate and optimize a lightweight machine-learning model for embedded deployment. Participants may apply suitable optimization techniques such as quantization and model compression and prepare their solution for deployment on the specified target platform.</p>\n<p>At the submission deadline, all submissions will be frozen. The organizing team will subsequently deploy and benchmark valid submissions on a standardized microcontroller platform using identical test conditions and hidden evaluation inputs.</p>\n<p><strong>Evaluation will be based on:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Performance / Accuracy &ndash; 45 points</li>\n<li>Inference Latency &ndash; 20 points</li>\n<li>Model Size / Resource Usage &ndash; 15 points</li>\n<li>Successful Edge Deployment &ndash; 10 points</li>\n<li>Technical Approach &amp; Documentation &ndash; 10 points</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The competition emphasizes practical Edge AI development and the engineering trade-offs involved in achieving strong model performance while meeting embedded hardware constraints.</p>\n<p><strong>Competition Duration:</strong> 2 hours<br /><strong>Team Size:</strong> 2&ndash;3 members<br /><strong>Domain:</strong> TinyML, Edge Computing &amp; Embedded AI</p>",
